  "conclusion": "On the idle Mac mini the same script, the same six-round B,C,C,B,B,C order and the same gates with relative_performance_gates=applied pass: parse ratios 0.969-1.001 (unclosed_4096 0.993), typeset medians 0.992/1.020/1.000 and best-of-3 1.131/1.010/0.991 for 32/128/512 formulas. The two CI attempts on a shared three-CPU runner disagreed with each other as much as with the local run: attempt 1 failed parse_unclosed_4096 at 1.328 (attempt 2 measured 1.106, a pass) and attempt 2 failed typeset-32/128 best-of-3 at 1.157/1.275 (attempt 1 measured 1.507/1.450), while ungated metrics in the same runs ranged 0.82-1.99. The round 9 diff changes only ConversationActivity.init and ConversationTodo, which the math preview never calls, and the check's own semantic gate (identical parsed semantics) passed in both attempts. The failures are treated as shared-runner noise on a tight best-of-3 threshold over a ~40ms measurement, not as a regression; no gate, threshold or assertion was modified, and the remedy was a rerun of the same head plus this local evidence.",
